#X obj 631 8 conv.degree2key;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 176 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object converts a scale degree to a key number (MIDI
note number in the current octave) \, using the selected scale. A scale
is defined as a sequence of intervals from the tonic \, and the degree
is the index of a step on this scale. The scale can be set with the
SCALE argument or the @scale property. The list of all supported scales
is available in the @all property.;
#X text 240 199 Note: some scales are not intended for the 12-tone
equal temperament.;
